    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To the rider: the $6.00 no-show charge stands and is not refunded; the driver is paid $4.80 of it, and $1.20 is retained as the platform service fee. This is decided on the driver's own instrument records, not on any finding about where you were.\n\nWhy the charge stands (POL-NS-01, POL-NS-02). The fee is chargeable only if all four limbs hold, and on EV-TRIP-00202 and EV-GPS-00202 they do. (a) The trip record carries a driver 'arrived' event at 23:13:10. (b) The GPS trace's first qualifying in-geofence fix is at 23:12:45, 25 seconds before that event, inside the 150 m Changi T3 AIRPORT arrival radius (POL-NS-02). (c) The driver then held position continuously inside that radius for 620 seconds, from 23:12:45 to 23:23:05, measured from the first qualifying fix as limb (c) directs, and the trace is 100% covered with no gaps; that is 140 seconds more than the 480-second free waiting period in force for this trip (trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec = 480). (d) The trip record shows no boarding and a termination by the driver at 23:23:20 under reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW, after the required dwell elapsed at 23:20:45; platform_policy.no_show_threshold_sec is unset. No clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces this: the qualifying fixes are inside the arrival radius, so POL-NS-03 (wrong entrance) does not apply; the arrival marker was not false, the driver being at his closest approach of 22.4 m and stationary at 23:13:10, so POL-NS-05 does not bite; and 620 seconds against 480 is a surplus, not a shortfall, so POL-NS-06 has nothing to refund.\n\nYour account, taken fully. (1) You say you were in the terminal the whole time. The GPS rider track cannot settle that either way: all 88 of your fixes report 45-80 m horizontal accuracy and are excluded by the 25 m filter, so under POL-NS-04(c) and POL-NS-11 your presence is UNDECIDABLE. I make no finding that you were elsewhere, and your device recording nothing admissible does not impair the driver's arrival or dwell. But your presence is not a condition of the fee, so this does not change the result. (2) You say you saw no messages until later. I accept that. The chat log EV-CHAT-00202 is impaired at weight 0.85 on issue UNREAD_MESSAGE: the system arrival notice at 23:13:11 and the driver's two messages at 23:14:02 and 23:19:30 were delivered but carry read_at null, so the record shows delivery, not receipt. But non-receipt does not exonerate you, because POL-NS-04 requires that YOU sent a locating or coordinating message that the driver then failed to answer within 120 seconds, and the log contains no message from you at all. POL-NS-06 states in terms that the fee turns on the driver's waiting time, not on whether the rider responded. (3) You did not press a dwell or a false-arrival attack, and rightly so on this arithmetic.\n\nThe driver's compensation (POL-NS-07). Compensation is 80% of the fee in force: 80% of $6.00 = $4.80, the same figure the fare breakdown EV-FARE-00202 derives. The anti-farming check reads only driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d (1, below 4) and completed_trips_30d (168, giving 1/168 = 0.006, below 0.08), so it does not trip and the payout is made. EV-DPROF-00202 is impaired at weight 0.90 on issue SCHEMA_VERSION_MISMATCH; that impairment is immaterial to those two counters, which sit far from both thresholds, and the finding survives the discount (POL-GEN-02(3)). No profile field outside the citable counters was used (POL-GEN-01).\n\nConfidence. The deciding facts of the charge and the payout are carried by the GPS trace (1.00), the trip record (1.00) and the fare breakdown (1.00); the lowest-weight artifact any part of this ruling rests on is the driver profile at 0.90, used only for the anti-farming check, so the cap is 0.90. That is above the 0.70 floor, so no escalation arises; the chat log's 0.85 bears only on receipt, which carries no deciding fact.\n\nThe monetary effect is $4.80, below the $8.00 execution threshold (POL-GEN-05), so it executes automatically. The driver's claim about the MISSING traffic advisory and the driver's claim that no POL-NS-09 trigger fires were discarded by the referee for citing impaired artifacts without naming their issue codes, and I do not rely on either. This ruling was made without human review and is provisional; either party may appeal within 30 days under POL-GEN-04."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

